# E769 draft - full pointer initialization in C++ tagged union
id:                     E769
trigger_tool:           test|runtime
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        killing signal catched|SIGSEGV.*Var::copy_value|invalid.*m_value.c

severity:               3
category:               ohos, aarch64, cpp, union, pointer-initialization
match_keywords:         wreport, Var, m_value, union, pointer, AArch64, SIGSEGV, memcpy
title:                  Zero the full pointer member of a mixed integer/pointer union

root_cause:             A value-initialized union initializes only its first member. When the first member is int32_t but later code reads char* from the same union, the pointer's upper bytes are not guaranteed to be zero on AArch64. A copy constructor then treats garbage m_value.c as allocated storage and writes through it.
affected_scope:         C++ packages that use an integer-first union as nullable pointer storage on 64-bit OHOS or other platforms.
verification_cmd:       conan create archives/w/wreport/3.36 --user=ohpcd --channel=stable -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           initialize-full-pointer-union-storage
rec_description:        Make the pointer member the first union member when the existing constructors use value initialization, or explicitly initialize the pointer member in every constructor. Preserve the union's external layout and verify copy, destruction, and full upstream tests on the target.
rec_command:            meson test -C build --print-errorlogs
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      explicit-pointer-member-initialization
fallback_description:   If changing the first union member is unsuitable, initialize m_value.c to nullptr explicitly in each constructor before allocate or copy_value can read it.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-patch

forbid_1_pattern:       ignore.*SIGSEGV|skip.*var.get_set|disable.*copy.*test
forbid_1_reason:        The crash is deterministic undefined behavior in real library copy semantics, not a flaky test.
forbid_1_consequence:   Consumer applications can crash while copying string-valued variables.

principles:             P013,P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

